# Styles

Styles used by only one component live next to it in a `*.module.css` file. Class names in a module are camelCase.

`src/app/global.css` holds only the theme: color tokens, typography, and constant spacing. Shared text states stay there too: `.sr`, `.muted`, `.status`, `.win`, `.loss`.

Do not copy repeated layout into feature modules. Put that layout in a component from `@/ui`.

```css
/* Bad: src/app/global.css owns a screen grid */
.records { display: grid; gap: 12px; }

/* Good: src/feature/record-cards/record-cards.module.css */
.records { display: grid; gap: 12px; }
```
